        "text": "This is a key difference between NFTs and other coins and tokens that are fungible. Being fungible means the coins and tokens are identical to each other, and therefore can serve as a medium for commercial transactions. Bitcoin and ether are fungible coins, for example. There are many more types of cryptocurrencies, but we can't cover them all in this module. A good place to start is to familiarize yourself with the biggest cryptos in terms of market capitalization first. From there, you can gradually explore the less mainstream altcoins. In the next module, let's look into centralized and decentralized crypto exchanges, where you can buy and sell cryptocurrencies.",
